  "description": "40 synthetic maintenance reports, 10 per language, written for Phase 8 as a held-out set: they were written from how technicians describe faults, not from the extraction rules, and were not used to tune the rules before the first measured run. Labels are what a maintenance engineer would record. 'category' lists every acceptable answer when the category is genuinely ambiguous. Priority is not hand-labelled: the evaluation applies the configured priority policy to the labelled fields and checks the pipeline reaches the same priority. Audio is generated from 'text' with Gnani Timbre (synthetic speech, not human recordings).",
  "fields": {
    "equipment": "registered code, or null when the code is missing or not in the register",
    "symptoms": "taxonomy keys (backend/app/intelligence/config/taxonomy.yaml)",
    "production_impact": "running | degraded | stopped | unknown (not stated)",
    "safety_concern": "true only when a hazard is explicitly reported (not negated)",
    "category": "list of acceptable categories",
    "next_action": "confirm_preview | ask_follow_up | fix_equipment"
  },
